WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.358 --> 00:00:16.027
"Ssss!" Kaa hissed as the monkeys ran in terror.

2
00:00:16.028 --> 00:00:19.798
Some of the monkeys had never met Kaa before.

3
00:00:19.799 --> 00:00:24.993
But they'd all heard stories about the terrifying python.

4
00:00:24.994 --> 00:00:30.487
He could slip along branches as quietly as moss grows.

5
00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:35.494
As the monkeys fled, Baloo drew in a deep breath of relief.

6
00:00:35.495 --> 00:00:38.780
He was sore and battered after fighting them.

7
00:00:38.781 --> 00:00:41.741
Bagheera was hurt too.

8
00:00:41.742 --> 00:00:47.679
The panther climbed out of the water tank and shook out his wet fur.

9
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.827
"Let's get Mowgli before those monkeys attack again," Bagheera said.

10
00:00:52.828 --> 00:00:58.020
"They will not attack again while I'm here!" Kaa hissed.

11
00:00:58.021 --> 00:01:01.150
"Where is the man cub anyway?"

12
00:01:01.151 --> 00:01:06.190
"In here!" Mowgli danced around inside the dome.

13
00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:08.659
"I'm trapped!"

14
00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:13.637
"Please get him out of here," said a snake at his feet.

15
00:01:13.638 --> 00:01:18.900
"He will crush our young."

16
00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:22.720
"Stand back, Mowgli," Kaa ordered.

17
00:01:22.721 --> 00:01:26.075
The python looked carefully at the dome.

18
00:01:26.076 --> 00:01:29.639
Finally he spotted a crack in the marble.

19
00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:37.304
Then, lifting his body high above the ground, he smashed down again and again.

20
00:01:37.305 --> 00:01:43.269
"Whoa!" Bagheera exclaimed as the marble shattered in a cloud of dust.

21
00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:48.434
Mowgli leaped out and threw himself at Baloo and Bagheera.

22
00:01:48.435 --> 00:01:52.865
"Are you okay?" Baloo asked.

23
00:01:52.866 --> 00:02:00.103
"I'm sore and hungry," Mowgli replied. "But I'm fine."

24
00:02:00.104 --> 00:02:02.419
Kaa stared at Mowgli.

25
00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:09.195
"So you're the man cub. Why, you look like a monkey!"

26
00:02:09.196 --> 00:02:16.296
Mowgli bowed. "Thank you for saving my life and my friends' lives."

27
00:02:16.297 --> 00:02:20.559
"It's nothing," Kaa said softly.

28
00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.698
By now the moon had sunk behind the hills.

29
00:02:24.699 --> 00:02:30.330
Trembling monkeys huddled together on the wall and along the stone buildings.

30
00:02:30.331 --> 00:02:39.425
Kaa glided into the center of the terrace and closed his jaws with a snap.

31
00:02:39.426 --> 00:02:43.847
Terrified, the monkeys watched him begin a slow dance.

32
00:02:43.848 --> 00:02:49.147
"This is my dance called the Hunger of Kaa.

33
00:02:49.148 --> 00:02:54.850
Sit still and watch me!" the snake commanded.

34
00:02:54.851 --> 00:02:59.426
Kaa wove his head from right to left.

35
00:02:59.427 --> 00:03:03.774
He made slow loops with his body.

36
00:03:03.775 --> 00:03:06.704
His scales rustled.

37
00:03:06.705 --> 00:03:09.675
Mowgli stood with Baloo and Bagheera.

38
00:03:09.676 --> 00:03:13.965
His eyes flicked from the monkeys to his friends.

39
00:03:13.966 --> 00:03:18.027
Everyone was watching the snake with wonder.

40
00:03:18.028 --> 00:03:25.020
Kaa hissed. "Come closer, monkeys . . ."

41
00:03:25.021 --> 00:03:28.584
The monkeys swayed forward helplessly.

42
00:03:28.585 --> 00:03:32.097
Baloo and Bagheera began to pitch forward too.

43
00:03:32.098 --> 00:03:34.799
Mowgli sprang toward them.

44
00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.054
"Come on!" he cried, yanking them away.

45
00:03:39.055 --> 00:03:41.574
"Let's get out of here!"

46
00:03:41.575 --> 00:03:47.414
The two great beasts jumped as if Mowgli had just woken them from a dream.

47
00:03:47.415 --> 00:03:54.212
Then they ran a short distance away.

48
00:03:54.213 --> 00:03:57.956
Bagheera glanced back at the snake and shuddered.

49
00:03:57.957 --> 00:04:02.054
"The monkeys aren't the only ones who are scared of Kaa.

50
00:04:02.055 --> 00:04:05.147
That snake makes me nervous."

51
00:04:05.148 --> 00:04:11.860
Baloo shook out his fur. "It worked out fine. We have Mowgli again."

52
00:04:11.861 --> 00:04:17.663
"True, but this little adventure cost us," Bagheera said sternly.

53
00:04:17.664 --> 00:04:22.737
"We're both injured. Which means we cannot hunt for several days.

54
00:04:22.738 --> 00:04:27.621
And we were forced to ask Kaa for protection."

55
00:04:27.622 --> 00:04:30.162
He glared at Mowgli.

56
00:04:30.163 --> 00:04:32.278
"We warned you about this.

57
00:04:32.279 --> 00:04:35.743
We told you it was foolish to play with the monkeys."

58
00:04:35.744 --> 00:04:41.549
Mowgli looked down. "I'm sorry."

59
00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.618
"He's very young," Baloo said.

60
00:04:44.619 --> 00:04:47.929
"And he's sorry for what he's done."

61
00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:56.356
"Being sorry is not enough punishment for breaking the rules!" Bagheera replied.

62
00:04:56.357 --> 00:05:01.375
With that, he gave Mowgli some light taps on the shoulder.

63
00:05:01.376 --> 00:05:06.823
"There," Bagheera said. "That's done."

64
00:05:06.824 --> 00:05:11.445
According to the law of the jungle, a punishment settled things.

65
00:05:11.446 --> 00:05:18.061
There was no need to say anything more about Mowgli's mistake with the monkeys.

66
00:05:18.062 --> 00:05:22.736
"Jump on my back, Little Brother," Bagheera said. "We will go home."

67
00:05:22.737 --> 00:05:31.461
"Okay." Mowgli climbed onto Bagheera's back and lay down his head.

68
00:05:31.462 --> 00:05:40.414
Soon he was fast asleep.
